"text": "SANCTUARY CITIES Sen. Jackson: Nay in 2025, Did Not Vote in 2024 → In 2025, Sen. Jackson voted against SB 21, a Republican bill that would take away governmental immunity from Georgia local governments that violate the state ban on sanctuary policies, and from sheriffs and jails that do not honor federal immigration detainer requests. In 2024, the Senate passed a rewrite of HB 301 that would also cut off certain state and federal funds to local governments found to violate that ban. She did not vote on it. Senate vote on SB 21, February 13, 2025: passed 33 to 18, Sen. Jackson Nay. The full House has not voted on it. Senate vote on the HB 301 substitute, March 21, 2024: passed 33 to 18, Sen. Jackson did not vote. Sources: legis.ga.gov vote records; Fox 5 Atlanta (March 6, 2024); The Advance News (February 12, 2025).",
"href": "https://www.fox5atlanta.com/news/georgia-bill-punish-immigrant-sanctuary-cities-counties"
